D did to Sarah as he had spoken. Sarah conceived, and bore Abraham a son in his old age, at the set time of which God had spoken to him.","canonicalTextHash":"135ddcf7d6f47d6ce2a0086aefc81be2cedcb33470afb239837017751ada94a2","citation":"Genesis 21:1–2","refId":"evidence:fa828b859667e16de4c31bbb","referenceHash":"fa828b859667e16de4c31bbb8458f0382d04edf25d9a087e6a52e9df615a742c","sourceIds":["engwebu:gen:21:1-2"]},{"canonicalText":"But I will establish my covenant with Isaac, whom Sarah will bear to you at this set time next year.”","canonicalTextHash":"90f2cfd98f063c9056699e84ea4914ce137db82a07b507b32366fa7fddda6beb","citation":"Genesis 17:21","refId":"evidence:5da954e8f33ec4d2507ef630","referenceHash":"5da954e8f33ec4d2507ef63072a22df4a7d7d1c3665ae7a55496a6ed77a8cb31","sourceIds":["engwebu:gen:17:21"]},{"canonicalText":"He said, “I will certainly return to you at about this time next year; and behold, Sarah your wife will have a son.” Sarah heard in the tent door, which was behind him.","canonicalTextHash":"baf9ad305ed201d752aacaa339bb375c1b92e1ed4e6b84d23851065e29e4765d","citation":"Genesis 18:10","refId":"evidence:3d8287839c633932f9346b98","referenceHash":"3d8287839c633932f9346b9868f65658877e819209fbfc7e9a139defd9f82d58","sourceIds":["engwebu:gen:18:10"]},{"canonicalText":"Is anything too hard for the LORD? At the set time I will return to you, when the season comes around, and Sarah will have a son.”","canonicalTextHash":"bb60c8f03dc082a8bf92e88c485cea6f747b9f743934366cefb9d113d06b44a7","citation":"Genesis 18:14","refId":"evidence:2e85c75eb9745fa6221fdf37","referenceHash":"2e85c75eb9745fa6221fdf37ef92a7bb54eada6a3fcd5b3794141a1fc99cc489","sourceIds":["engwebu:gen:18:14"]}],"findings":[{"canonicalEvidence":"The LORD visited Sarah as he had said, and the LORD did to Sarah as he had spoken. Sarah conceived, and bore Abraham a son in his old age, at the set time of which God had spoken to him.","canonicalEvidenceHash":"135ddcf7d6f47d6ce2a0086aefc81be2cedcb33470afb2398